  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 255 PM CDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\nThe cooler, fall-like conditions continue into Monday and early next \nweek with highs generally only reaching the upper 50s to near 60 \nboth Monday and Tuesday. Our light rain generally continues into \nMonday, this time with a bit more synoptic support as a an upper \nlevel low meanders into Iowa trudging along in the zonal upper level \nflow. This low hangs out overhead into Tuesday, but begins to \nbring drier air into the state. Should this pan out as the \nmodels suggest, we should finally see a few dry days Tuesday and\nWednesday of next week. However, rain chances do look to return\nto at least western Iowa on Thursday. More details on that in \nthe coming days.",
